erized provider-extra coupling test (RED on Dockerfile.opcert), then declared --extra bedrock in Dockerfile.opcert; targeted test now passes.","timestamp":1788739306726425001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Committed implementation in exec-e46b at 5158eea82387; verify-commit-ticket passed. Running make verify next.","timestamp":1788739488738692001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify passed in exec-e46b; pushing to Gerrit for LLM-Review and Verified.","timestamp":1788743284493639001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2729 reached LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1 with no unresolved comments, then was submitted/merged. Updating worktree and closing ticket.","timestamp":1788745767203227001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Checked acceptance criteria after Gerrit change 2729 merged as 04a50980f9b1 and local make verify passed.","timestamp":1788746084191947001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787868854620124001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"18cb744c-e033-49f2-a3ed-b1b88d44fb35","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d43e-c24f-dd39-44e9"},{"link_uuid":"dd096db9-9449-4925-8daa-4018c7c3f0dd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"44b5-d05c-0e26-4f93"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered by the Step-7 sibling sweep while fixing bug facial-lunar-urson (the deployed MCP\nimage ran Bedrock-configured LLM gates with no Bedrock provider installed).\n\n`infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert:39` builds with:\n\n```\nRUN uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra reviewbot\n```\n\nThere is **no `--extra bedrock`**, yet this image runs the real LLM gates:\n`src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py:68-76` dispatches `review_plan` and `verify_completion`,\nand its docstring states the defaults \"call the real LLM\". With `rebar.toml:198-199` pinning\n`bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`, that is the same construct as the fixed bug.\n\n## Why it is NOT currently broken (and why it should still change)\n\nThe provider import succeeds today **incidentally**: `pyproject.toml:93` defines\n`reviewbot = [\"fastapi\", \"uvicorn[standard]\", \"boto3\"]`, and boto3 is the only thing\npydantic-ai-slim's `bedrock` extra actually contributes. So an extra that exists for the\nCloudWatch publish path is what keeps the Bedrock provider importable here.\n\nThe project has already ruled on exactly this situation in the sibling image.\n`infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot` declares `--extra bedrock` and its comment says so\nexplicitly: \"DECLARED FOR EXPLICITNESS, NOT TO FIX A MISSING IMPORT... Naming `bedrock` makes\nthe dependency INTENTIONAL and lock-enforced. Without it, dropping boto3 from the `reviewbot`\nextra — or pydantic-ai-slim later adding a bedrock-extra dependency beyond boto3 — would break\nthe provider at gate time in production.\" `Dockerfile.opcert` is the remaining image that has\nnot had that ruling applied.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd `--extra bedrock` to `Dockerfile.opcert`'s `uv sync` line, with a comment pointing at the\nsame rationale, and extend the coupling guard added for facial-lunar-urson in\n`tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` (or a peer test) so it covers every image that runs LLM\ngates, not just `Dockerfile.mcp`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert` installs the `bedrock` extra and states why.\n- [x] A test asserts the provider-extra coupling for EVERY gate-running image\n      (`Dockerfile.mcp`, `Dockerfile.reviewbot`, `Dockerfile.opcert`), shown RED for\n      `Dockerfile.opcert` before the change.\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the infra contract suites pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert","reason":"declare --extra bedrock so the Bedrock provider dependency is intentional and lock-enforced rather than incidentally satisfied by the reviewbot extra boto3"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py","reason":"extend the configured-provider/installed-extra coupling guard to cover every gate-running image"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","44b5-d05c-0e26-4f93"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"bfe5909e-4a0a-489a-9d07-b5430cebfc5d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e46b-9ca3-d1b3-4dd4","ticket_type":"task","title":"Declare the bedrock extra in Dockerfile.opcert — the op-cert gate service runs real LLM gates but satisfies the Bedrock provider only incidentally","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c64742f9-f587-4645-9b23-f2060533bd38","be497a57-508c-467d-9c0d-98ba17c98bf0","0c67a5e4-306b-4630-9f51-edeba7c6a0ab","4ff460a8-6a3f-4b92-bacc-081146acdc2d","ca5b7fa1-3665-41de-b415-bce7e611e2e4","076daad3-e37b-4629-bb1f-3130ce69b0a3","ae1a79ff-09ef-47f6-8550-03cbf4c76b25","ebbb142e-64b7-42f1-8e7d-fed785b7f28b","dd096db9-9449-4925-8daa-4018c7c3f0dd","caba0c4e-62f6-4ad3-8cab-5c039be1339f","21f7336b-ee89-4e50-be92-0e9e634d9c94","82c799cb-1020-4a05-9bf6-0dfd20b4e06a","bfe5909e-4a0a-489a-9d07-b5430cebfc5d","1ebeebc0-5522-4658-8462-a2ac67dd9e84"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788751244383210001,"uuid":"9fc0ff40-3d07-46e4-a4ee-103acbf1ae82"}